Body:
> I just faced the same issue, and simply I just went to a new session and tested the model, and the model was responding perfectly. The issue was the context window. I think they're limiting the context window, and I reached around 45%, and this happened.

Do you have a config file set up for auto-compaction and the context window?

{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  "compaction": {
    "auto": true,
    "prune": true,
    "reserved": 150000
  },

  "provider": {
    "openrouter": {
      "models": {
        "stealth/ox-alpha": {
          "limit": {
            "context": 1048576,
            "output": 131072
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

This PR enables sorting of repos in the UI, of local repo clones of the repo -in general-, and of the sessions within each local repo clone within the repo.

For instance, Claude App now filters all sessions of the repo regardless of which local repo clone the session is under.  With Claude App, it's not immediately obvious which local clone the session (of a specific repo) is operating.  I'm not suggesting this, this and other ways of sorting/filtering are now options for the UI.  The UI work is, obviously, for a different and future PR (based on this being merged).

@Hona @Brendonovich OpenCode is losing paid subs over this PR (or other solution to the problem) not being merged.
